  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}\\frac{18}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =18{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{-3})]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =-6\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{{a}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{{3}^{3}}) \\\\  & =-6(0-\\frac{1}{27}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
